WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.029
The idea of someone fluffing up their resume
with made-up stuff might sound like something

00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:06.209
straight out of a sitcom…

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.100
"I don't have to say anything.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.600
I'm a doctor too."

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.500
...but there have been plenty of actors who've
been caught red-handed using made-up achievements

00:00:14.509 --> 00:00:16.390
to get onto the red carpet.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.580
Here are just a few actors who've lied to
get the part.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.090
Laura Fraser

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:26.690
When the producers of AMC's hit series Breaking
Bad asked actress Laura Fraser (I apologize

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:30.539
to any German's watching this) "Sprichst du
Deutsch?" she answered with an unequivocal

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:31.539
"Ja!"

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:35.930
The truth was, though, that Fraser had barely
any experience with German — unlike her

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.440
character, the conniving, anxious, stevia-loving
Lydia Rodarte-Quayle.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.350
She didn't regret the decision, but she did
have to eat her words later when she was handed

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.550
a full paragraph of German dialogue...and
had to wing it.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.860
(German speaking clip from Breaking Bad)

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.210
Fraser told The Daily Mail,

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.080
"It was corporate-speak German, and it was
a nightmare.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.320
It took me days to learn a little paragraph."

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.880
The benefit, apart from the fact that she
got the role, of course?

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.930
"Now I bore my family with it — it's my
party trick."

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.260
Eddie Redmayne

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:06.371
Now that he's an Oscar winner, Eddie Redmayne
probably doesn't have to use a phony bio to

00:01:06.371 --> 00:01:07.859
get his role of choice.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:12.429
But once upon a time, he was an up-and-comer
who would say and do anything to score a key

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:13.429
part.

00:01:13.429 --> 00:01:17.289
When he went out for the British TV series
Elizabeth I, Redmayne claimed to be able to

00:01:17.289 --> 00:01:19.469
ride a horse when, well, he couldn't.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.079
"woooooooeeeeeoooooooaaaa"

00:01:25.079 --> 00:01:29.830
After casually lying to director Tom Hooper
and being given a scene on horseback two weeks

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.210
later, the truth came out.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.759
As he remembered to Vanity Fair,

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.490
"I gave my horse a nudge and it went off at
a hundred miles an hour … I was sent to

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.890
horse camp immediately."

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:41.500
Hooper must not have minded the deception
too much because he also hired Redmayne for

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.770
his big screen adaptation of Les Miserables
and his 2015 film, The Danish Girl.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.460
Hooper may have gotten a little payback, though,
by having Redmayne jump on horseback with

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.770
a flag during Les Mis, said Redmayne.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.070
"That was my penance.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.729
My payback for that lie to him years ago."

00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:58.299
Carla Gugino

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:03.499
When she was 16, Carla Gugino nabbed her first
film role in Troop Beverly Hills by claiming

00:02:03.499 --> 00:02:05.030
that she was just 14.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:08.649
She didn't confess until later in the shoot,
when her role was already safe.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:11.410
She recounted the event to talk show host
James Corden.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:14.250
"I told the director like three weeks in,
once I knew I couldn't get fired 'cause we'd

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.250
shot enough.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.410
I was like, 'Just so you know, I am 16.'

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:19.500
I thought for sure he was gonna be like, 'No
big deal,' but he was like, 'I would've never

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.670
hired you if I knew you were 16.'"

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:26.250
With that, Gugino learned her lesson about
lying, and vowed she's never done it again.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.440
Whoopi Goldberg

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.370
Born Caryn Elaine Johnson, Whoopi Goldberg's
stage name is just part of the image adjustment

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.510
that went into giving the award-winner her
start in entertainment.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.810
Early on in her illustrious career, she had
to fake being older in order to nab worthy

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.450
roles, because she was seen as too young for
showbiz.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:48.570
On her resume, she switched her year of birth
from 1955 to 1949, later explaining to The

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.570
Daily News:

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.950
"I lied about my age for a long time because
nobody would hire me to act.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:53.950
Everyone said I was too young.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:56.970
So, when I was 20, I put six years on my life."

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:01.620
Unfortunately, starring in Theodore Rex put
another ten years on Whoopi's life as well.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:07.450
(Whoopi Goldberg flirts with a dinosaur)

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.040
George Lazenby

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:14.090
Australian model George Lazenby had almost
no screen experience when he convinced producers

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.580
that he was qualified to step into Sean Connery's
swanky shoes as James Bond.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.380
"My name's Bond, James Bond."

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.110
"The new bond!"

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:27.540
Equipped with a false bio and a whole lot
of bravado, Lazenby made it all the way to

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:32.100
an audition for the role in front of director
Peter Hunt when he finally came clean about

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.380
his false credentials.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:37.090
The bold move impressed Hunt so much that
he was willing to overlook the truth.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:40.290
Lazenby told The New York Post that Hunt swore
him to secrecy, saying,

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.290
"What?

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.290
And you say you can't act?

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:45.430
You've fooled two of the most ruthless men
I've ever met in my life.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:48.020
Stick to your story, and I'll make you the
next James Bond."

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:52.220
Lazenby starred in On Her Majesty's Secret
Service, and was even contracted for many

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.350
more Bond films.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:57.410
But he bowed out due to creative differences,
returning the role to Sean Connery.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.840
"Who are you?"

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:02.000
"My name is Bond, James Bond."

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.910
Lazenby, Connery...doesn't matter.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.640
Because we can all agree that Daniel Craig's
the best, right guys?

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.650
Right?

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.460
"I like that James Bond is ugly now!"

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.320
"I like that he doesn't have any gadgets!"

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:17.010
"I like that he's not good at shooting, doesn't
say funny quips, or do any James

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.010
Bond stuff!"

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.560
Just kidding Timothy Dalton all the way!

